<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  The eleven small dialogs of spec.md 15b's dialogs.xrc entry:
  set_start_dlg, resume_dlg, exit_running_dlg
  (xrc-windows.md section B),
  edit_crossing_dlg, manual_deal_dlg, dnf_confirm_dlg,
  void_card_confirm_dlg (section C), about_dlg, selftest_dlg,
  shortcuts_dlg (section E), crossing_detail_dlg (section F, J2).
  stop_confirm_dlg (section B) retired in W5: the Stop flow now asks
  through the native confirm (ui.std_dialogs.show_confirm) instead of
  an XRC dialog.
  no_ride_dlg (section B) retired in W15: the store-backed launch that
  resumes nothing and opens nothing now shows nothing at all; the
  console stands and the create/open choice is the File menus' own
  job.
  Phase 11 (H2) retired four more section-B dialogs for native
  std_dialogs: finish_confirm_dlg (show_danger, with the REOPENED
  "Finish again" label), duplicate_ride_dlg and reopen_ride_dlg
  (show_prompt), and exit_confirm_dlg (show_confirm). Their copy
  moved to views/dialogs.py and quit_flow.py respectively.
  Control names are frozen; tests find them with
  FindWindowByName and tools/gen_ids.py turns them into ui/ids.py
  (R-05, R-73). Names repeat across these windows on purpose -
  plate_input, reason_input and continue_btn each appear in more than
  one - because spec.md 15b requires uniqueness only within a
  top-level window.

  Measured on wxPython 4.3.1 / wxWidgets 3.3.3:

    * wxStdDialogButtonSizer only *places* the ids its AddButton()
      recognises - wxID_OK/YES/SAVE, wxID_APPLY, wxID_NO,
      wxID_CANCEL/CLOSE, wxID_HELP/CONTEXT_HELP. Any other button is
      still created as a child of the dialog, so it resolves by name,
      but it is never added to the sizer: GetContainingSizer() is None
      and it stays at (-1,-1). void_btn, continue_btn,
      library_btn and rerun_btn therefore sit in a sibling wxBoxSizer,
      the shape crossing_detail_dlg already uses.
    * <default>1</default> is honoured on wxButton, inside a std sizer
      or a box sizer; the dialog's GetDefaultItem() returns it.
      <focused>1</focused> is declared alongside it on the destructive
      confirms but could NOT be verified here: a terminal-launched,
      unbundled Python never becomes the frontmost macOS application,
      so no window takes key focus and even an explicit SetFocus()
      leaves FindFocus() at None. The functional suite has to assert
      initial focus against an activated app.
      Measured on windows-latest (Phase 10): MSW GetDefaultItem()
      follows the focused control - or the first-declared button when
      nothing is focused - and <default>1</default> alone is NOT
      honoured there. Every intended default therefore also carries
      <focused>1</focused>, which is what spec.md 13's initial-focus
      rules ask for anyway.
    * <wrap>420</wrap> is honoured on wxStaticText and is what keeps
      the three long confirm paragraphs from Fit()ing to a single
      700-940 px line. wxStaticText::Wrap() rewrites the label with
      newlines, so anything that later calls SetLabel on one of these
      has to re-wrap; they are all fixed wording, so nothing does.
    * XRC cannot give one control both a custom name and a stock id
      value: the id comes from the name attribute, and the
      name="foo=5100" form is not parsed by this build (XRCID returns
      a generated value and the window name keeps the literal "=5100").
      The canvas marks continue_btn as wxID_OK in resume_dlg; the
      frozen name wins here and the affirmative behaviour is code-side -
      SetAffirmativeId(XRCID("continue_btn")).
    * wxDataViewListCtrl cannot be authored here: its XRC handler
      hard-forces the control name to "dataviewCtrl". shortcuts_list is
      a wxDataViewCtrl, whose name IS honoured.
    * wxHyperlinkCtrl needs both a label and a url; constructing it
      with neither trips a C++ assertion that aborts the interpreter,
      so gorba_link declares both.
    * <font><family>teletype</family></font> gives selftest_output a
      genuinely fixed-width face (IsFixedWidth() is True) without
      naming a font or a point size, so it still follows system
      metrics and the 90-150% zoom.
    * XRC has no minsize property for windows - only for sizeritem and
      wxSplitterWindow (wxWidgets src/xrc/xmlres.cpp SetupWindow). None
      of these dialogs has a documented minimum, so none declares a
      <size> and the sizer handler Fit()s it and applies
      SetSizeHints(). selftest_output declares a control-level <size>
      because a multi-line text area has no useful best size of its
      own.

  Recorded gap (resolved): the dialogs that write live data into a
  message line — resume_dlg's ride name (the wording swapping for a
  crash) and delete_ride_dlg's ride name (library.xrc) — were
  declared as unnamed, empty wxStaticText and could not be written
  to until the frozen-name registry gained message_lbl; E5.2.3
  registered it (spec §15b) and every such dialog now declares it.

  Code-side per the canvas: edit_crossing_dlg is one resource with two
  titles - Cards > Edit Crossing and Cards > Add Crossing at Time set
  the title and prefill the fields, and void_btn is shown in edit mode
  only; every message and data label's text; selftest_output's report;
  shortcuts_list's rows, generated from the single accelerator table so
  they cannot drift.
-->
<resource>

  <!-- ============================ section B ============================ -->

  <object class="wxDialog" name="set_start_dlg">
    <title>Set Start Time</title>
    <!-- R-05 requires resizable windows; the in-app text zoom (90-150%)
         cannot work in a fixed-size dialog. spec.md 13 says "dialogs
         fixed-size" - recorded conflict, resolved in favour of R-05.
         The same style is on every dialog in this file; about_dlg is
         the sole exception (ux-polish fixed size, see its own block). -->
    <style>wxDEFAULT_DIALOG_STYLE|wxRESIZE_BORDER</style>

    <object class="wxBoxSizer">
      <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxBoxSizer">
          <orient>wxHORIZONTAL</orient>
          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL|wxRIGHT</flag>
            <border>8</border>
            <object class="wxStaticText">
              <label>Started at</label>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL|wxRIGHT</flag>
            <border>6</border>
            <object class="wxDatePickerCtrl" name="start_date_picker"/>
          </object>
          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
            <object class="wxTimePickerCtrl" name="start_time_picker"/>
          </object>
        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStaticText">
          <label>Lap-1 times recompute from this moment.</label>
        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxALL</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStdDialogButtonSizer">
          <object class="button">
            <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_OK">
              <default>1</default>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="button">
            <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_CANCEL"/>
          </object>
        </object>
      </object>

    </object>
  </object>

  <!-- Two buttons, neither of which is an id wxStdDialogButtonSizer
       places, so this dialog has no std sizer at all: library_btn is
       the secondary and continue_btn the primary, ordered left to
       right per spec.md 13. -->
  <object class="wxDialog" name="resume_dlg">
    <title>Resume Ride</title>
    <style>wxDEFAULT_DIALOG_STYLE|wxRESIZE_BORDER</style>

    <object class="wxBoxSizer">
      <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>

      <!-- The ride name, and wording that swaps for a crash restart
           (session_state). Written by the presenter. -->
      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStaticText" name="message_lbl">
          <label></label>
        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxALL</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxBoxSizer">
          <orient>wxHORIZONTAL</orient>

          <object class="spacer">
            <option>1</option>
            <size>0,0</size>
          </object>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL|wxRIGHT</flag>
            <border>6</border>
            <object class="wxButton" name="library_btn">
              <label>Open library</label>
            </object>
          </object>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
            <object class="wxButton" name="continue_btn">
              <label>Continue ride</label>
              <default>1</default>
              <focused>1</focused>
            </object>
          </object>

        </object>
      </object>

    </object>
  </object>

  <object class="wxDialog" name="exit_running_dlg">
    <title>Ride Is Running</title>
    <style>wxDEFAULT_DIALOG_STYLE|wxRESIZE_BORDER</style>

    <object class="wxBoxSizer">
      <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <!-- E5.2.3: the message line carries the frozen name message_lbl
             (spec §15b's shared name, also in resume_dlg) so the exit
             path can interpolate the running
             ride's name into it; the label below is the fallback copy
             the smoke test screenshot renders, and app.py overwrites it
             with the ride-naming copy before ShowModal. -->
        <object class="wxStaticText" name="message_lbl">
          <label>Quitting won't stop the ride — it keeps timing on the wall clock, and you'll be asked to continue when you reopen.</label>
          <wrap>420</wrap>
        </object>
      </object>

      <!-- Three buttons per spec §3, §15 and R-51: Cancel · Finish ride
           first… · Quit-keep-running. The canvas draws only two; the
           requirements are the acceptance authority and this is missing
           functionality, not styling, so the third button stays.
           Order is §13's Ghost · Secondary · Primary.
           finish_first_btn sits outside the wxStdDialogButtonSizer
           because Realize() positions only the ids it recognises. A
           custom button placed inside it is created but left at
           (-1,-1). Cancel keeps the default so a reflex Enter is safe
           (R-76: destructive confirms focus Cancel). -->
      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxALL</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxBoxSizer">
          <orient>wxHORIZONTAL</orient>

          <object class="spacer">
            <option>1</option>
            <size>0,0</size>
          </object>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL|wxRIGHT</flag>
            <border>6</border>
            <object class="wxStdDialogButtonSizer">
              <object class="button">
                <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_CANCEL">
                  <default>1</default>
                  <focused>1</focused>
                </object>
              </object>
            </object>
          </object>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL|wxRIGHT</flag>
            <border>6</border>
            <object class="wxButton" name="finish_first_btn">
              <label>Finish ride first…</label>
            </object>
          </object>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
            <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_OK">
              <label>Quit — keep ride running</label>
            </object>
          </object>

        </object>
      </object>

    </object>
  </object>

  <!-- ============================ section C ============================ -->

  <object class="wxDialog" name="edit_crossing_dlg">
    <title>Edit Crossing</title>
    <style>wxDEFAULT_DIALOG_STYLE|wxRESIZE_BORDER</style>

    <object class="wxBoxSizer">
      <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxFlexGridSizer">
          <cols>2</cols>
          <vgap>6</vgap>
          <hgap>8</hgap>
          <growablecols>1</growablecols>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
            <object class="wxStaticText">
              <label>Plate</label>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxEXPAND</flag>
            <object class="wxTextCtrl" name="plate_input"/>
          </object>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
            <object class="wxStaticText">
              <label>Crossing time (clock)</label>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxEXPAND</flag>
            <object class="wxTimePickerCtrl" name="time_picker"/>
          </object>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
            <object class="wxStaticText">
              <label>Reason</label>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxEXPAND</flag>
            <object class="wxTextCtrl" name="reason_input"/>
          </object>

        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxALL</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxBoxSizer">
          <orient>wxHORIZONTAL</orient>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
            <object class="wxButton" name="void_btn">
              <label>Void crossing…</label>
            </object>
          </object>

          <object class="spacer">
            <option>1</option>
            <size>0,0</size>
          </object>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
            <object class="wxStdDialogButtonSizer">
              <object class="button">
                <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_OK">
                  <default>1</default>
                </object>
              </object>
              <object class="button">
                <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_CANCEL"/>
              </object>
            </object>
          </object>

        </object>
      </object>

    </object>
  </object>

  <object class="wxDialog" name="manual_deal_dlg">
    <title>Deal Bonus Card</title>
    <style>wxDEFAULT_DIALOG_STYLE|wxRESIZE_BORDER</style>

    <object class="wxBoxSizer">
      <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxFlexGridSizer">
          <cols>2</cols>
          <vgap>6</vgap>
          <hgap>8</hgap>
          <growablecols>1</growablecols>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
            <object class="wxStaticText">
              <label>Plate</label>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxEXPAND</flag>
            <object class="wxTextCtrl" name="plate_input"/>
          </object>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
            <object class="wxStaticText">
              <label>Reason</label>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxEXPAND</flag>
            <object class="wxTextCtrl" name="reason_input"/>
          </object>

        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStaticText">
          <label>Deals the next card from the shoe — deterministic, audit-logged.</label>
        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxALL</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStdDialogButtonSizer">
          <object class="button">
            <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_OK">
              <label>Deal</label>
              <default>1</default>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="button">
            <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_CANCEL"/>
          </object>
        </object>
      </object>

    </object>
  </object>

  <object class="wxDialog" name="dnf_confirm_dlg">
    <title>Mark DNF</title>
    <style>wxDEFAULT_DIALOG_STYLE|wxRESIZE_BORDER</style>

    <object class="wxBoxSizer">
      <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>

      <!-- Phase 3: the target is typed in (a pooled rider's plate, or
           a whole entry's plate), so this dialog no longer needs an
           entry to be open first. entry_lbl carries the consequence
           copy; when a target is already known (the entry-detail
           button, a menu route with an open entry) the runner
           overwrites it with the naming sentence
           (dialogs.dnf_message). plate_input comes first so it is the
           form's initial focus (views/dialogs.py FORM_FIRST_FIELDS). -->
      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxBoxSizer">
          <orient>wxHORIZONTAL</orient>
          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL|wxRIGHT</flag>
            <border>8</border>
            <object class="wxStaticText">
              <label>Rider plate</label>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="sizeritem">
            <option>1</option>
            <flag>wxEXPAND</flag>
            <object class="wxTextCtrl" name="plate_input"/>
          </object>
        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStaticText" name="entry_lbl">
          <label>Excluded from the results; a team keeps its other riders.</label>
        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxBoxSizer">
          <orient>wxHORIZONTAL</orient>
          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL|wxRIGHT</flag>
            <border>8</border>
            <object class="wxStaticText">
              <label>Reason</label>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="sizeritem">
            <option>1</option>
            <flag>wxEXPAND</flag>
            <object class="wxTextCtrl" name="reason_input"/>
          </object>
        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxALL</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStdDialogButtonSizer">
          <object class="button">
            <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_OK">
              <label>Mark DNF</label>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="button">
            <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_CANCEL">
              <default>1</default>
              <focused>1</focused>
            </object>
          </object>
        </object>
      </object>

    </object>
  </object>

  <!-- E7 mock-first: Void Card… confirm (spec.md §15). Authored in E7 with
       its control names registered in §15b before any UI wiring, replacing
       the E1.4.1 _UNAUTHORED_DIALOG sentinel. -->
  <object class="wxDialog" name="void_card_confirm_dlg">
    <title>Void Card</title>
    <style>wxDEFAULT_DIALOG_STYLE|wxRESIZE_BORDER</style>

    <object class="wxBoxSizer">
      <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>

      <!-- The card being voided and the entry it belongs to, in the same
           two-column caption/data grid crossing_detail_dlg uses. Both cells
           are code-written (run_void_card), never blank (UX-DESKTOP §4). -->
      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxFlexGridSizer">
          <cols>2</cols>
          <vgap>6</vgap>
          <hgap>8</hgap>
          <growablecols>1</growablecols>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
            <object class="wxStaticText">
              <label>Card</label>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
            <object class="wxStaticText" name="card_lbl">
              <label></label>
            </object>
          </object>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
            <object class="wxStaticText">
              <label>Entry</label>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
            <object class="wxStaticText" name="entry_lbl">
              <label></label>
            </object>
          </object>
        </object>
      </object>

      <!-- The consequence, below the grid and above the Reason row; fixed
           wording and stays in XRC. -->
      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStaticText">
          <label>Removes the card from the entry's scored hand. Audit-logged.</label>
        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxBoxSizer">
          <orient>wxHORIZONTAL</orient>
          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL|wxRIGHT</flag>
            <border>8</border>
            <object class="wxStaticText">
              <label>Reason</label>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="sizeritem">
            <option>1</option>
            <flag>wxEXPAND</flag>
            <object class="wxTextCtrl" name="reason_input"/>
          </object>
        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxALL</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStdDialogButtonSizer">
          <object class="button">
            <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_OK">
              <label>Void card</label>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="button">
            <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_CANCEL">
              <default>1</default>
              <focused>1</focused>
            </object>
          </object>
        </object>
      </object>

    </object>
  </object>

  <!-- ============================ section E ============================ -->

  <object class="wxDialog" name="about_dlg">
    <title>About RiverCrossing</title>
    <!-- Fixed-size (ux-polish): the About box's short fixed copy must
         never wrap from a user resize, so it alone drops
         wxRESIZE_BORDER; AboutDialog pins ABOUT_SIZE code-side.
         Every other dialog in this file keeps wxRESIZE_BORDER for the
         90-150% text zoom (R-05). -->
    <style>wxDEFAULT_DIALOG_STYLE</style>

    <object class="wxBoxSizer">
      <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>

      <!-- "RiverCrossing 1.0.9" - the product name plus the package
           version, written by AboutDialog. -->
      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_HORIZONTAL|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStaticText" name="version_lbl">
          <label></label>
        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_HORIZONTAL|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStaticText">
          <label>Timing &amp;&amp; poker-hand scoring for poker-run rides.</label>
        </object>
      </object>

      <!-- ux-polish: the three fixed attribution lines below the
           tagline; fixed wording, so it stays in XRC like the
           tagline above. -->
      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_HORIZONTAL|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStaticText" name="author_lbl">
          <label>Mark Buckaway</label>
        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_HORIZONTAL|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStaticText" name="copyright_lbl">
          <label>© 2026 Mark Buckaway</label>
        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_HORIZONTAL|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStaticText" name="license_lbl">
          <label>Licensed under GPL-3.0-only</label>
        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_HORIZONTAL|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxBoxSizer">
          <orient>wxHORIZONTAL</orient>
          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL|wxRIGHT</flag>
            <border>4</border>
            <object class="wxStaticText">
              <label>Built for GORBA —</label>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
            <object class="wxHyperlinkCtrl" name="gorba_link">
              <label>gorba.ca</label>
              <url>https://gorba.ca</url>
            </object>
          </object>
        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxALL</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStdDialogButtonSizer">
          <object class="button">
            <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_CLOSE">
              <default>1</default>
            </object>
          </object>
        </object>
      </object>

    </object>
  </object>

  <object class="wxDialog" name="selftest_dlg">
    <title>Evaluator Self-Test</title>
    <style>wxDEFAULT_DIALOG_STYLE|wxRESIZE_BORDER</style>

    <object class="wxBoxSizer">
      <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>

      <!-- The report is dot-leadered, so it only lines up in a
           fixed-width face. "teletype" asks for the system's monospace
           family rather than naming one, which keeps the control
           native and lets it follow the text zoom. -->
      <object class="sizeritem">
        <option>1</option>
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxTextCtrl" name="selftest_output">
          <style>wxTE_MULTILINE|wxTE_READONLY</style>
          <size>420,140</size>
          <font>
            <family>teletype</family>
          </font>
        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxALL</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxBoxSizer">
          <orient>wxHORIZONTAL</orient>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
            <object class="wxButton" name="rerun_btn">
              <label>Run again</label>
            </object>
          </object>

          <object class="spacer">
            <option>1</option>
            <size>0,0</size>
          </object>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
            <object class="wxStdDialogButtonSizer">
              <object class="button">
                <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_CLOSE">
                  <default>1</default>
                </object>
              </object>
            </object>
          </object>

        </object>
      </object>

    </object>
  </object>

  <object class="wxDialog" name="shortcuts_dlg">
    <title>Keyboard Shortcuts</title>
    <style>wxDEFAULT_DIALOG_STYLE|wxRESIZE_BORDER</style>

    <object class="wxBoxSizer">
      <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <option>1</option>
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxDataViewCtrl" name="shortcuts_list"/>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxALL</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStdDialogButtonSizer">
          <object class="button">
            <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_CLOSE">
              <default>1</default>
            </object>
          </object>
        </object>
      </object>

    </object>
  </object>

  <!-- ============================ section F ============================ -->

  <!-- J2: the read-only Crossing Detail dialog, opened by double-clicking
       a row of the console's crossings feed. The nine value fields are
       read-only entry boxes, empty here and written by
       views/crossing_detail.py's CrossingDetailView with SetValue (the
       view-model is code-side, like every other DataView/label content
       on this canvas). They sit in one "Details" group as four columns
       in a row (G2: caption, value, caption, value), and the captions
       are fixed copy carrying no frozen name. The plate is
       read-only copy too, in crossing_plate_lbl, so edit_btn, which
       says "Edit Plate", opens the §9 Plate prompt instead of an
       editable field here, and every correction re-renders this dialog
       in place: OK is the one control that closes it (Delete closes it
       too, its crossing being gone).

       edit_btn, edit_time_btn, void_card_btn and delete_btn sit in a
       sibling wxBoxSizer beside the stock button sizer:
       wxStdDialogButtonSizer positions only
       OK/Yes/Save/Apply/No/Cancel/Close/Help, so a custom button placed
       inside it is created but left at (-1,-1) (measured). edit_time_btn
       opens edit_crossing_dlg in edit mode and void_card_btn voids the
       crossing's own credited card (Phase 2: the corrections the
       retired Reassign Plate…/Void Card… menu rows used to reach). The
       stock sizer carries wxID_OK alone: a Cancel beside it would be a
       second control that closes the window, which the dialog is
       deliberately not offering, so the view points Escape at OK with
       SetEscapeId, wx's own Escape handling (measured) only ever
       looking for wxID_CANCEL. -->
  <object class="wxDialog" name="crossing_detail_dlg">
    <title>Crossing Detail</title>
    <style>wxDEFAULT_DIALOG_STYLE|wxRESIZE_BORDER</style>

    <object class="wxBoxSizer">
      <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStaticBoxSizer">
          <label>Details</label>
          <orient>wxHORIZONTAL</orient>

          <!-- The four columns of G2: caption, value, caption, value.
               A caption column carries no <option> and no width, so it
               auto-sizes to its longest label; the read-only column
               beside it keeps its own 180 px, with an 8 px right border
               between every pair.

               The two columns are separate sizers, so nothing aligns
               their rows for them: measured at 100% zoom, a caption
               stands 16 px tall and a read-only box 24 px, so the
               captions take a 14 px bottom border against the boxes'
               6 px and both columns hold a 30 px row stride. The 6 px
               keeps the flex grid's own vgap this sizer replaces. -->

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxRIGHT</flag>
            <border>8</border>
            <object class="wxBoxSizer">
              <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>

              <object class="sizeritem">
                <flag>wxBOTTOM</flag>
                <border>14</border>
                <object class="wxStaticText">
                  <label>Rider</label>
                </object>
              </object>

              <object class="sizeritem">
                <flag>wxBOTTOM</flag>
                <border>14</border>
                <object class="wxStaticText">
                  <label>Team</label>
                </object>
              </object>

              <object class="sizeritem">
                <flag>wxBOTTOM</flag>
                <border>14</border>
                <object class="wxStaticText">
                  <label>Plate</label>
                </object>
              </object>

              <object class="sizeritem">
                <flag>wxBOTTOM</flag>
                <border>14</border>
                <object class="wxStaticText">
                  <label>Lap #</label>
                </object>
              </object>

              <object class="sizeritem">
                <flag>wxBOTTOM</flag>
                <border>14</border>
                <object class="wxStaticText">
                  <label>Crossing time</label>
                </object>
              </object>

            </object>
          </object>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxRIGHT</flag>
            <border>8</border>
            <object class="wxBoxSizer">
              <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>

              <object class="sizeritem">
                <flag>wxEXPAND|wxBOTTOM</flag>
                <border>6</border>
                <object class="wxTextCtrl" name="crossing_rider_lbl">
                  <style>wxTE_READONLY</style>
                  <size>180,-1</size>
                  <value></value>
                </object>
              </object>

              <object class="sizeritem">
                <flag>wxEXPAND|wxBOTTOM</flag>
                <border>6</border>
                <object class="wxTextCtrl" name="crossing_team_lbl">
                  <style>wxTE_READONLY</style>
                  <size>180,-1</size>
                  <value></value>
                </object>
              </object>

              <object class="sizeritem">
                <flag>wxEXPAND|wxBOTTOM</flag>
                <border>6</border>
                <object class="wxTextCtrl" name="crossing_plate_lbl">
                  <style>wxTE_READONLY</style>
                  <size>180,-1</size>
                  <value></value>
                </object>
              </object>

              <object class="sizeritem">
                <flag>wxEXPAND|wxBOTTOM</flag>
                <border>6</border>
                <object class="wxTextCtrl" name="crossing_lap_lbl">
                  <style>wxTE_READONLY</style>
                  <size>180,-1</size>
                  <value></value>
                </object>
              </object>

              <object class="sizeritem">
                <flag>wxEXPAND|wxBOTTOM</flag>
                <border>6</border>
                <object class="wxTextCtrl" name="crossing_time_lbl">
                  <style>wxTE_READONLY</style>
                  <size>180,-1</size>
                  <value></value>
                </object>
              </object>

            </object>
          </object>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxRIGHT</flag>
            <border>8</border>
            <object class="wxBoxSizer">
              <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>

              <object class="sizeritem">
                <flag>wxBOTTOM</flag>
                <border>14</border>
                <object class="wxStaticText">
                  <label>Lap time</label>
                </object>
              </object>

              <object class="sizeritem">
                <flag>wxBOTTOM</flag>
                <border>14</border>
                <object class="wxStaticText">
                  <label>Total time</label>
                </object>
              </object>

              <object class="sizeritem">
                <flag>wxBOTTOM</flag>
                <border>14</border>
                <object class="wxStaticText">
                  <label>Card</label>
                </object>
              </object>

              <object class="sizeritem">
                <flag>wxBOTTOM</flag>
                <border>14</border>
                <object class="wxStaticText">
                  <label>Status</label>
                </object>
              </object>

            </object>
          </object>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <object class="wxBoxSizer">
              <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>

              <object class="sizeritem">
                <flag>wxEXPAND|wxBOTTOM</flag>
                <border>6</border>
                <object class="wxTextCtrl" name="crossing_lap_time_lbl">
                  <style>wxTE_READONLY</style>
                  <size>180,-1</size>
                  <value></value>
                </object>
              </object>

              <object class="sizeritem">
                <flag>wxEXPAND|wxBOTTOM</flag>
                <border>6</border>
                <object class="wxTextCtrl" name="crossing_total_lbl">
                  <style>wxTE_READONLY</style>
                  <size>180,-1</size>
                  <value></value>
                </object>
              </object>

              <object class="sizeritem">
                <flag>wxEXPAND|wxBOTTOM</flag>
                <border>6</border>
                <object class="wxTextCtrl" name="crossing_card_lbl">
                  <style>wxTE_READONLY</style>
                  <size>180,-1</size>
                  <value></value>
                </object>
              </object>

              <object class="sizeritem">
                <flag>wxEXPAND|wxBOTTOM</flag>
                <border>6</border>
                <object class="wxTextCtrl" name="crossing_held_lbl">
                  <style>wxTE_READONLY</style>
                  <size>180,-1</size>
                  <value></value>
                </object>
              </object>

            </object>
          </object>

        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxALL</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxBoxSizer">
          <orient>wxHORIZONTAL</orient>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL|wxRIGHT</flag>
            <border>6</border>
            <object class="wxButton" name="edit_btn">
              <label>Edit Plate</label>
            </object>
          </object>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL|wxRIGHT</flag>
            <border>6</border>
            <object class="wxButton" name="edit_time_btn">
              <label>Edit Time…</label>
            </object>
          </object>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL|wxRIGHT</flag>
            <border>6</border>
            <object class="wxButton" name="void_card_btn">
              <label>Void Card…</label>
            </object>
          </object>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL|wxRIGHT</flag>
            <border>6</border>
            <object class="wxButton" name="delete_btn">
              <label>Delete</label>
            </object>
          </object>

          <!-- Absorbs the row's slack so the stock button sizer, the
               last item, stays right-aligned however wide the dialog
               is (rider_issues_dlg's spacer pattern). -->
          <object class="spacer">
            <option>1</option>
            <size>0,0</size>
          </object>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
            <object class="wxStdDialogButtonSizer">
              <object class="button">
                <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_OK">
                  <label>OK</label>
                  <default>1</default>
                  <focused>1</focused>
                </object>
              </object>
            </object>
          </object>

        </object>
      </object>

    </object>
  </object>

  <!-- J2/§9: the Crossing Detail Edit prompt. Edit is the "wrong plate
       on the line" correction, so it asks for the plate in a small
       Save/Cancel dialog rather than unlocking the detail window's own
       read-only plate field; OK still commits that field, but only
       miss mode unlocks it. The one field is a plain wxTextCtrl sized
       for the four digits a plate at most carries (main.xrc's own
       <hint>), with a real persistent caption beside it, never
       placeholder text (UX-DESKTOP §7). Save is the marked default so
       Enter commits and Escape keeps the stock Cancel route; the
       stock sizer and stock ids give both for free (UX-DESKTOP §3). The
       view (views/crossing_detail.py's run_plate_dialog) seeds
       number_input with the crossing's current plate, focuses and
       selects it, and reads Save's trimmed text; nothing here resolves
       the plate, since RideEngine.reassign_crossing owns the refusal. -->
  <object class="wxDialog" name="crossing_number_dlg">
    <title>Plate</title>
    <style>wxDEFAULT_DIALOG_STYLE|wxRESIZE_BORDER</style>

    <object class="wxBoxSizer">
      <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxFlexGridSizer">
          <cols>2</cols>
          <vgap>6</vgap>
          <hgap>8</hgap>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
            <object class="wxStaticText">
              <label>Plate</label>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
            <object class="wxTextCtrl" name="number_input">
              <size>50,-1</size>
            </object>
          </object>

        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxALL</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStdDialogButtonSizer">
          <object class="button">
            <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_OK">
              <label>Save</label>
              <default>1</default>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="button">
            <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_CANCEL">
              <label>Cancel</label>
            </object>
          </object>
        </object>
      </object>

    </object>
  </object>

</resource>
